  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electronic Processing and One-Stop Shop for Construction Permits</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the project is to improve the business environmentby reducing the cost and time of procedures for dealing with construction permits through simplification and automation of these procedures. #    #   The specific areas of focus include: (i) business process reengineering (BPR)to streamline the review process for construction permits and establish one-stop-shop (OSS) service delivery; (ii) introducing electronic system (ready for integration with centralized unified property database of state cadastre, geographic information system (GIS) , and other relevant authorities) for choosing from existing model samples or uploading new design documentation, as well as formal review and approval; and (iii) introducing model design samples (including for SME infrastructure) and enabling further enhancement of the collection of standarddesign packages by municipalities. TF012782</narrative>
  </description>
